Confluence is planning authority. Repository `docs/` mirrors must not invent conflicting requirements.

## Planned SDK / build constraints

* minSdk 26
* compileSdk 36
* targetSdk 36
* Gradle JDK 21
* JVM target 17
* Firebase-first backend (Auth, Firestore, Storage, FCM, App Check)
* Auth: Google Sign-In + Email/Password
* Monetization: Ads + Premium (isolated modules)

Do not claim Android implementation is complete until the relevant Tasks and quality gates are Done.

## Workflow (mandatory)

`To Do → In Progress → In Review → Done`

* To Do → In Progress only after Task preflight passes
* In Progress → In Review only after validation passes **and** the PR is open
* Done only after human merge **and** post-merge validation on `origin/develop`
* Testing is an In Progress / post-merge gate — not a separate Jira status
* Do **not** self-merge PRs
* Do **not** move to Done without real evidence
* Never fabricate PR numbers, commit hashes, test results, or release evidence

## One Task / one branch

* Execute only the assigned Task; do not start HAP-14+ (or any other Task) unless explicitly instructed
* One implementation Task in Progress/In Review at a time unless a human explicitly directs otherwise
* Branch formats:
  * Implementation: `task/HAP-<n>-kebab-summary`
  * Docs (when specified): `docs/HAP-<n>-kebab-summary`
* Always branch from latest `origin/develop` (not stale local `develop` / `main`)
* Never commit directly to `main` or `develop`
* Push only the Task branch

## Validation before PR

* Satisfy the Task acceptance criteria and repository validation checklist
* Prefer existing project linters/tests; do not install unrelated global tools
* Keep diffs scoped to the Task; do not stage unrelated or user-owned untracked files

## After PR open

* Comment evidence on the Jira Task (branch, commit, PR URL/number, base/head, validation, scope)
* Move In Progress → In Review
* Stop and wait for human review unless the human explicitly continues

## Preserve user / untracked files

* Identify untracked or user-owned files during preflight
* Do not stage, modify, delete, or commit them unless the Task explicitly owns them

## Secrets and production config

Forbidden in git and docs:

* API keys, tokens, passwords
* `google-services.json` / Firebase production identifiers
* Keystores, keystore passwords, signing configs with secrets
* Production endpoint credentials

Use secret managers / local ignore patterns when configuration Tasks arrive.

## Medical safety

* Record, do not diagnose or prescribe
* Never silently alter, calculate, or round dose text
* Tapering requires explicit steps
* Duplicate-dose: warn + acknowledge; retain conflicting Given evidence on sync
* No ads on critical medical-safety surfaces
* Serious reactions: direct caregivers to seek veterinary care

## Accessibility

* TalkBack labels and focus order on primary flows
* Large font / dose readability
* Contrast; do not convey critical state by color alone

## Offline / sync / duplicate-dose

* Room (local) is source of truth for critical care data when offline architecture is implemented
* Queue durable mutations; surface conflicts; never last-write-wins for dose Given events
* Airplane-mode critical reads (today / med due / emergency cache) are required by NFR offline rules

## Quality gates and release

* Exactly one Quality Gate Task per Epic (see Project Plan)
* Publish `docs/test-reports/<epic-key>-test-report.md` at each Epic QG — no fabricated content
* Internal release only after HAP-12 quality gate and Completion Report process
* Completion Report remains **Template — Not Yet Completed** until a real release completion Task fills it

## Design handoff (HAP-19)

* HAP-19 gates Tasks needing final approved UI/design assets
* Do not treat Figma as approved for UI implementation before HAP-19 is Done
* Do not modify Figma unless the active Task explicitly requires it

## Stop conditions

Stop and report (no speculative fixes outside scope) when:

* Preflight fails
* Tracked files have unexpected conflicting user changes
* Required dependencies are not Done
* Another implementation Task is already In Progress or In Review
* Secrets would be required to proceed
* Scope would expand into a later Task (for example HAP-14+)
* PR checks or human review block progress

## Cursor rules location

HappyPaws execution policy lives in this repository under `.cursor/rules/`. Do not create global Cursor rules outside the repo for this project's workflow authority.
